    "rules": "Eligible rows are nonabandoned and nonmetalinguistic single-span giver moves labelled instruct; 4 through 24 lexical reference words, first to last word duration 2 through 10 seconds. Require at least one published named landmark (full canonical name as contiguous words within a linked annotated surface span inside that move) and a listed relation. No other channel annotated spoken word overlaps the source interval padded 0.12 seconds on both sides. Do not inspect ASR or take results. Sort competing moves by ascending SHA256(seed|dialogue|move id) then case ID. First allocate between, then the remaining relation vocabulary with no word between. Retain any quotas not reached; never replace a poor result or failed audio retrieval.",
    "audio_extraction": "HTTP range read the original stereo PCM WAV header and bytes covering floor/ceil 0.12 second padded times from transcript (both channels). Preserve original sampling rate and quantization; write new WAV container only. Source WAV range bytes and final WAV hashed separately. Capture errors or impossible ranges as deficits. Cap network to 80 MiB including XML.",
    "model": "Existing verified Systran/faster-whisper-small.en, pinned local release defaults, CPU int8. No prompt, hotwords, adaptation, retries of recognition, transcript correction or outcome filtering for scores.",
    "asr_metrics": "Word edits and corpus WER with the project's lowercased English tokenization; exact sentence; relation tokens correct in order by longest common subsequence, extras and complete-sequence exactness; number of named mentions correctly transcribed exactly in annotated order. A failed recognition counts as an empty delivered hypothesis. Publish per-case numeric counts and hashes, plus totals, no raw speech/text.",
    "application": "Open a fresh session on the actual local passenger webpage for each WAV. The scene is a known nonfinal Gulf photograph used only as the UI backdrop. Audio must appear in the editable review textbox, source WAV and transcription receipts must match hashes. Validate lack of proposal/confirmation on upload; edit the field to the published words (scripted repair only), validate equivalent ordinary voice request contract, and cancel the unmatched map turn. No model call or proposal, map spatial result, passenger approval, or simulated original speaker consent is credited.",
    "team_intake": "Separate project collection requires explicit project-specific consent, S01-S03, 10 fixed scene scripts per individual, listenback and verification; external corpus does not supply these. Do not open private team WAVs or replies."
  },
